        "original_id": "bbe65e3a-556c-5b0d-b57b-15d61d2674bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Rūmī, Farouk El-Baz\n- Roles: poet, jurist, Islamic scholar, theologian, Sufi mystic, space scientist\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Projects: Apollo missions\n- Topics: lunar exploration, astronaut training\n\nFacts:\n- Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Rūmī was born on 30 September 1207 and died on 17 December 1273.\n- Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Rūmī was also known as Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Balkhī, Mevlânâ or Mawlānā, Mevlevî or Mawlawī, and Rumi.\n- Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Rūmī was a 13th-century Persian Sunni Muslim poet, jurist, Islamic scholar, theologian, and Sufi mystic.\n- Farouk El-Baz was born on January 2, 1938.\n- Farouk El-Baz is an Egyptian American space scientist.\n- Farouk El-Baz worked with NASA on planning scientific exploration of the Moon, including selecting Apollo mission landing sites and training astronauts in lunar observations and photography.",
